Browser Context Architecture (Very Important)

One browser can have multiple isolated sessions.

Example:

Browser
 ├── Context 1 (User A)
 ├── Context 2 (User B)
 └── Context 3 (Admin)

Benefits:

Faster parallel execution
Multi-user testing
Session isolation
Less memory usage

Playwright architecture is designed around direct browser communication using native browser protocols
instead of external WebDrivers. The Playwright client communicates with a Playwright driver/server, which directly controls browser engines like Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. It also supports isolated browser contexts, built-in synchronization, 
auto-waiting, network interception, and parallel execution, making it faster and more stable than Selenium for modern web applications
